; In-tree unit + property tests for smt/theories/lia. Depends only on oxsmt_core and
; oxsmt_lia, so it honors the dependency firewall (I3) even though it lives under smt/.
; Run via `make lia-test`; also built by `make build`.
;
; The independent Farkas verifier and the brute-force enumerator here are deliberately
; test-only and written from the certificate/semantics definitions (DESIGN §10), not from
; the solver internals.

(executable
 (name lia_test)
 (modules lia_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_lia))

; The THEORY-adapter test (ADR-0005 M4). Same firewall: oxsmt_core + oxsmt_lia only. Its
; independent Farkas verifier reconstructs half-planes from the adapter's PUBLIC premise
; literals (no engine internals), per DESIGN §10.

(executable
 (name lia_adapter_test)
 (modules lia_adapter_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_lia))

; Bigint self-test (core-bignum W2): hand vectors + pure-OCaml property vectors + an
; INDEPENDENT Python differential oracle (R4). The oracle shells out via stdlib
; [Sys.command]; no library dep is added, so the I3 firewall holds. python3-absent → skip.

(executable
 (name bigint_test)
 (modules bigint_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_lia))

; One-word (Zarith-style) Rational representation self-test: rep-boundary vectors +
; INDEPENDENT Python fractions.Fraction differential oracle crossing the immediate/block
; boundary both ways. Simplex-free (so it always terminates) — the mutation-testing suite
; for the rational-word mutants. Same I3 firewall; python3-absent → skip.

(executable
 (name rational_word_test)
 (modules rational_word_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_lia))

; Standalone HNF kernel self-test (Stage B lattice kernel): hand matrices, a random
; property sweep (self-check + an independent unimodularity witness), the lattice-
; determinant invariant, and a modular/ring-lattice gcd example. oxsmt_core + oxsmt_lia
; only (I3 firewall).

(executable
 (name hnf_test)
 (modules hnf_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_lia))
